00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:16.130
- There's a gap between who
people are, and what they

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:17.780
tell you they want to accomplish.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:29.730
- Okay, let's kick it
off with Rule Number One:

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:32.250
Don't Let Obstacles Break You.

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:34.573
- As Confucius said, "When it's obvious

00:01:34.573 --> 00:01:36.767
"that the goal cannot be reached,

00:01:36.767 --> 00:01:40.836
"don't adjust the goals,
adjust the action steps."

00:01:40.836 --> 00:01:44.825
That may be the single best
piece of advice you're ever

00:01:44.825 --> 00:01:45.819
going to get.

00:01:45.819 --> 00:01:47.043
Write that down.

00:01:47.043 --> 00:01:49.031
Burn it into your flesh.

00:01:49.031 --> 00:01:50.507
Tattoo it on your soul.

00:01:50.507 --> 00:01:52.240
Do whatever you need to do

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:56.150
to remember that once you
set a goal, once you've

00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:59.610
decided in your life, there
is something that you're

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:03.450
going to make come true,
don't let anything stop

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:04.914
you from reaching that.

00:02:04.914 --> 00:02:06.570
But the reality is as you

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:07.493
go things are going to get in your way.

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:12.095
There will be an inevitable
slew of obstacles coming at you.

00:02:12.095 --> 00:02:15.420
But when it gets so hard
that you realize that the

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.560
path that you're on simply
is not going to take you

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:21.100
where you want to go,
rather than give up on what

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:23.830
it was you said you were going
to do, find a different path.

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:26.040
And in that when you really make that

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:29.490
the cornerstone of your
identity, that you refuse to bend

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:33.350
or be broken by obstacles,
by challenges, but instead

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:36.310
you rise to those challenges,
you go over, under,

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:38.100
through them, you do whatever you have to

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:42.453
you devise any plan to find a way through,

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:45.250
then your life will change.

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:46.930
Once that becomes your

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:50.780
reaction to not change that
thing that meant so much to you,

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:51.960
that you've dedicated your life

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:54.580
to making it come true,
that you don't change that

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:56.910
but rather you find another
way, you tap into your

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.860
creativity, you find
somebody that can help you,

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:01.080
you do whatever it takes
to get on the other side

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:05.673
of that, you do whatever
it takes to build that life

00:03:05.673 --> 00:03:07.423
that you want to see.

00:03:07.423 --> 00:03:09.500
But if your reaction

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:12.490
is to change your goal, to make it easier,

00:03:12.490 --> 00:03:16.265
to move it closer, to be
less of who you could be,

00:03:16.265 --> 00:03:18.753
simply so you could check a box.

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:22.250
You're never going to have
anything that's worth having.

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:23.260
- Rule Number Two:

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:24.618
Take the First Step.

00:03:24.618 --> 00:03:27.340
- Why, like if you had to boil it down,

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:28.813
why do most people fail?

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:31.567
Got it locked?

00:03:31.567 --> 00:03:34.453
The answer is they never start.

00:03:35.967 --> 00:03:38.710
Now the reason that
most people never start

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:42.020
is because they don't
think they're going to get

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:44.880
a result from their actions
and then that's going

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:47.787
to come down to a belief that
they believe about themselves.

00:03:47.787 --> 00:03:49.508
"I'm too stupid."

00:03:49.508 --> 00:03:51.227
"I'm not good enough."

00:03:51.227 --> 00:03:53.187
"I don't have the natural talent."

00:03:53.187 --> 00:03:55.407
"I wasn't born at the right time

00:03:55.407 --> 00:03:56.427
"or in the right neighborhood."

00:03:56.427 --> 00:03:58.127
"My parent's didn't teach me that"

00:03:59.922 --> 00:04:02.127
That's why most people fail.

00:04:02.127 --> 00:04:03.860
There's a great quote

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:06.573
by Amelia Earhart, I'll paraphrase.

00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:09.900
The hard thing is taking the first step,

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:13.510
everything else is just persistence.

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:15.520
And I've always loved that
quote because it's so true.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:16.840
It doesn't mean that you're
going to get it right,

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:18.055
it doesn't mean that
just because you start

00:04:18.055 --> 00:04:19.050
you're going to win.

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:20.260
In fact, most likely,

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:21.680
the first thing you do,
you're going to fail.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:23.860
Speak about all the times
that you tried something

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:24.693
and it failed.

00:04:24.693 --> 00:04:25.526
The first time when you tried to get

00:04:25.526 --> 00:04:26.880
the business going and it didn't work.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:28.490
Or the first house you
tried to sell and nobody

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:29.928
went for it, or the first
time that you lost money.

00:04:29.928 --> 00:04:32.330
And the question is, what did you do then?

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:34.830
If you learned from it,
doubled down, figured it out

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:38.920
focused only on the truth,
then you moved forward.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.540
You move forward because
you believe you can learn

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:43.340
And that's that thing, hiding in that,

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:45.741
and this is the thing when
people ask me, hey my mom

00:04:45.741 --> 00:04:50.741
or my wife or whatever, they
don't have that belief system.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.769
They don't have what Carol
Dweck calls a growth mindset.

00:04:53.769 --> 00:04:55.580
How do I get them there?

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:56.830
The answer is you don't.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:58.780
Until they are convinced

00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:01.105
that they can learn anything
that they put their mind to,

00:05:01.105 --> 00:05:02.990
that their energy is doubled down into

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:06.200
that area of gaining skills
will actually pay off.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:09.720
With a real world ability
to do something new,

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:11.330
they're not going to act.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:12.430
- Rule Number Three:

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:14.100
Out-work Everyone.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:16.270
- Coby Bryant, one of the
greatest athletes of our

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:21.270
time, would show up on game
day and if he saw anybody

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:25.670
else at the gym as early
as him, even though he was

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:29.190
always the first on the court,
he would end up practicing

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:30.386
longer than that person.

00:05:30.386 --> 00:05:31.700
And I had the honor

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:33.953
of interviewing one of
those people one time.

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:37.877
And he said, "I went up and
asked Coby, Coby we have

00:05:37.877 --> 00:05:40.077
"a game in an hour, like
what are you doing out here

00:05:40.077 --> 00:05:41.210
"practicing so long?"

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:42.637
And Coby said "I needed you to know

00:05:42.637 --> 00:05:44.487
"that I was willing to out-work you."

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:47.728
And in that game they
ended up winning, and that

00:05:47.728 --> 00:05:50.183
lesson stuck with that guy forever.

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:54.630
When you're willing to put in the work,

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:56.290
when you're willing to take control of

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:58.750
your environment and
put yourself through the

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:01.287
stressors required for
adaptation, you literally

00:06:01.287 --> 00:06:02.954
can become anything.

00:06:02.954 --> 00:06:06.060
And my life is proof of that.

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:07.190
- Rule number Four:

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:08.640
Prepare for the Luck.

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:10.470
- I hear people talk about luck a lot.

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:12.110
And I know that people
think about the role

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:13.650
that luck plays in their life.

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:16.625
But the reality is, luck is all around,

00:06:16.625 --> 00:06:17.910
luck is ever present.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:20.350
Luck literally is coming to you every day,

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:21.320
it's passing you by.

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:23.753
It's happening to you right now.

00:06:23.753 --> 00:06:25.080
But the question is, are you able

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:26.868
to take advantage of the luck?

00:06:26.868 --> 00:06:28.800
Have you prepared for the luck?

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:30.670
And I think that it comes down to,

00:06:30.670 --> 00:06:33.370
we have a misconception
about what luck is.

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:35.790
We think of luck as
something being passive,

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:37.888
that we sit, we wait,
we're in some obscure place

00:06:37.888 --> 00:06:41.320
and still somehow the luck find us.

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:44.040
But the reality is we're awash in luck.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:48.070
What we're missing is the
ability to make use of it.

00:06:48.070 --> 00:06:49.810
If you have a bunch of bullets but no gun

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:50.800
you really have nothing.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:51.650
If you have a gun but no

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:52.770
bullets, the same thing.

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:54.810
The magic moment comes

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:56.780
together when you have
two things that work

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:59.800
in conjunction and you have them both.

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:02.680
You can't have luck without the diligence.

00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:05.020
You can't have success without the skills.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:08.180
You've got to spend your life preparing

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:09.841
to capitalize on that luck.

00:07:09.841 --> 00:07:11.100
And to look at what

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:13.220
somebody has done, to look
at a moment of success

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:15.460
in their life and to say that it was luck,

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:18.800
is to create a frame of reference
for you in which you can't

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:21.611
see how you yourself could
leverage what you have

00:07:21.611 --> 00:07:23.350
to get lucky.

00:07:23.350 --> 00:07:24.320
- Rule Number Five:

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:26.690
Find Deep Fulfillment.

00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:28.690
- One thing I want to make really clear.

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:32.300
And if you ignore everything
else, this is the one

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:33.800
where you stop and pay attention.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:36.333
Because this could save
years of your life.

00:07:38.142 --> 00:07:42.683
The game you're playing is not success,

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:47.090
the game you're playing is not money,

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:49.623
the game you're playing
is brain chemistry.

00:07:50.795 --> 00:07:53.700
The only thing that
matters in life, truly,

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:55.990
the only thing that matters in life,

00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:58.630
is what you think about
yourself when you're

00:07:58.630 --> 00:08:01.833
by yourself and have nothing
but your own thoughts.

00:08:03.640 --> 00:08:06.770
If in that moment you feel
good about who you are,

00:08:06.770 --> 00:08:09.770
who you're becoming,
what you're capable of,

00:08:09.770 --> 00:08:11.670
and what you're willing
to do to make a better

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:15.300
future for yourself, those
you care about and other

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:19.620
people around you, you
will love your life.

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:24.060
It is the single most
pleasurable neuro-chemical

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:26.227
state is deep fulfillment.

00:08:26.227 --> 00:08:27.630
Okay?

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:28.670
Not happiness.

00:08:28.670 --> 00:08:29.960
A bowl of ice cream brings me a lot

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:34.780
of happiness, but it is a
very transient experience.

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:36.640
Deep and lasting fulfillment matters.

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:38.730
And what that comes down
to is how you feel about

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:40.560
yourself when you're by yourself.

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:41.520
- Rule Number Six:

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:43.310
Know Your Why.

00:08:43.310 --> 00:08:45.430
- The piece of advice that
I always give to somebody,

00:08:45.430 --> 00:08:47.300
whether it's an entrepreneur
or somebody who wants

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:49.263
to be the greatest parent of all time.

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:53.573
What is your goal?

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:57.640
You've got to start with your goal.

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:01.010
Everything works backwards from that.

00:09:01.010 --> 00:09:03.410
Simon and I did a video
that essentially broke

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:05.493
the Internet about millennials.

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:07.847
Somebody watched it.

00:09:07.847 --> 00:09:09.650
(audience members laugh)

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:12.540
What got Simon on the
world stage is his whole

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:14.120
concept of why?.

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:16.190
You've got to know why you're

00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:18.144
doing what you're doing.

00:09:18.144 --> 00:09:20.260
If you're just showing up

00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:23.960
every day to cut and
dye hair, to keep your

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:27.130
lights on, you're going
to have far less energy

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:29.520
to make it through the
hard times than somebody

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:31.610
who is there to help transform somebody,

00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:35.243
to make somebody their best,
to help them feel their best.

00:09:35.243 --> 00:09:37.580
And I hope that you guys saw that

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:39.570
video not too long ago
of the hairdresser that

00:09:39.570 --> 00:09:42.548
went around and he was doing
makeovers on homeless people.

00:09:42.548 --> 00:09:43.770
(audience claps)

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:44.650
Right?

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:48.160
Man, it was incredible.

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:52.380
It was so beautiful,
the look on their face

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:54.912
at that moment when they
see themselves for the first

00:09:54.912 --> 00:09:57.010
time in front of the
mirror and they are seeing

00:09:57.010 --> 00:09:57.926
something totally new.

00:09:57.926 --> 00:09:59.009
They are seeing a version

00:09:59.009 --> 00:10:01.703
of themselves that they
did not know was there.

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:05.590
And the ability to give
that gift, like it is so

00:10:05.590 --> 00:10:07.990
easy to get lost in the
day-to-day grind of what

00:10:07.990 --> 00:10:11.450
you do, what any of us
do, but if at the core

00:10:11.450 --> 00:10:14.150
driving you is a deep and unending why

00:10:14.150 --> 00:10:16.700
for what you're doing,
you've got something.

00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:20.353
Now you've got a chance to
transcend what you're doing.

00:10:20.353 --> 00:10:22.550
And the way that happens is very tactical,

00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:25.060
it has nothing to do with
being woo-woo being out there.

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:25.893
It's none of that.

00:10:25.893 --> 00:10:27.330
You're going to have the energy

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:28.810
that you need to fight through.

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:29.970
- Rule Number Seven:

00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:31.330
Protect Your Vision.

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:33.920
- We get to decide who we are.

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:35.440
There's no objective truth

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:37.320
that you're going to find or uncover.

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:39.010
You are simply the collection

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:42.280
of the things you believe
to be true about yourself.

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:44.395
And once you begin to form that opinion

00:10:44.395 --> 00:10:48.870
of who you are, you'll act in
accordance with that belief.

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:51.410
You begin to shape a vision of yourself

00:10:51.410 --> 00:10:55.523
in your own mind and
that becomes the reality.

00:10:56.864 --> 00:10:58.230
So letting other people influence that,

00:10:58.230 --> 00:11:00.720
letting other people
come in and degrade what

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:04.060
you think of yourself, is
one of the most dangerous

00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:05.480
and damning things you could do.

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:08.860
Because they cloud your ability to craft.

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:13.140
To craft a vision of the
person that you want to become.

00:11:13.140 --> 00:11:15.270
And that vision is so hard for all

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:17.060
of us to hold on to that
we have to protect it.

00:11:17.060 --> 00:11:19.640
We have to keep other people out of that.

00:11:19.640 --> 00:11:23.210
We've got to have intention in creating

00:11:23.210 --> 00:11:24.820
the person that we want to become.

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:25.870
- Rule Number Eight:

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:27.090
Get Better.

00:11:27.090 --> 00:11:30.610
- You are all hopelessly average by birth.

00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:31.443
We all are.

00:11:31.443 --> 00:11:33.430
And that's the great news.

00:11:33.430 --> 00:11:36.140
Because the most important
thing to understand

00:11:36.140 --> 00:11:38.500
about the human species

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:40.993
we are the ultimate adaptation machine.

00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:43.373
If you guys were paying attention

00:11:43.373 --> 00:11:46.400
not too long ago they
sequenced the human genome

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:51.190
and they realized that the
human genome has 20,000 genes.

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:52.360
And everybody they thought

00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:54.540
that they were going to cure
cancer, all the diseases,

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:58.700
AIDS related disease, everything,
Type 1, Type 2 diabetes.

00:11:58.700 --> 00:11:59.870
It was all going to be
a thing of the past.

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:01.260
We were going to have it figured out.

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:04.469
And then we realized that
an onion has more genetic

00:12:04.469 --> 00:12:06.093
diversity than we do.

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:08.230
And how could that be?

00:12:08.230 --> 00:12:09.260
And so they're literally going,

00:12:09.260 --> 00:12:10.170
is this really possible?

00:12:10.170 --> 00:12:11.233
Did we misunderstand something?

00:12:11.233 --> 00:12:14.551
How is it that an onion
has more genetic diversity

00:12:14.551 --> 00:12:15.634
than we have?

00:12:15.634 --> 00:12:18.650
And somebody finally said,

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:20.450
hey maybe all this stuff
that we've been referring

00:12:20.450 --> 00:12:24.170
to as junk DNA, maybe it
actually plays a role.

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:26.430
And then they began to
realize that all that

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:29.910
junk DNA that was outside
of those 20,000 genes

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:31.610
that we saw expressing themselves,

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:34.421
is what is called epigenetics.

00:12:34.421 --> 00:12:35.830
Now if you've ever heard

00:12:35.830 --> 00:12:38.080
of epigenetics that's
amazing, you're way ahead.

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:39.923
If you haven't heard of epigenetics,

00:12:40.912 --> 00:12:41.810
let it become one of the
most important things

00:12:41.810 --> 00:12:45.839
in your life because
epigenetics is what has made

00:12:45.839 --> 00:12:50.810
us the most dominant species
this planet has ever seen.

00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:52.760
It is the only thing
that you need to know.

00:12:52.760 --> 00:12:55.730
It's what I call the
only belief that matters.

00:12:55.730 --> 00:13:00.393
The only belief that matters
is that you can learn anything.

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:03.220
I don't need you to believe
that you're good now.

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:04.053
That doesn't matter.

00:13:04.053 --> 00:13:06.210
Who you are now is totally irrelevant.

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:08.610
The only thing I want to
know, who are you willing

00:13:08.610 --> 00:13:10.290
to become and what's
the price you're willing

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:11.203
to pay to get there?

00:13:11.203 --> 00:13:13.710
And that's what humans are designed to do.

00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:18.550
If you put us under stress,
we can learn something new.

00:13:18.550 --> 00:13:20.100
We can get better.

00:13:20.100 --> 00:13:21.160
- Rule Number Nine:

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:23.467
Turn Negatives Into Positives.

00:13:23.467 --> 00:13:25.087
- "What are some ways that I can stop

00:13:25.087 --> 00:13:27.210
"giving this negative feedback to myself?"

00:13:27.210 --> 00:13:30.230
Okay so, first of all
you've got to train yourself

00:13:30.230 --> 00:13:34.130
to use the negative
thoughts that you have as a

00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:36.320
habit loop trigger of something positive.

00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:38.650
That's the first step to all of this.

00:13:38.650 --> 00:13:41.980
So I don't think anybody
is going to be able

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:43.352
to get rid of the negative
voice, and even if you

00:13:43.352 --> 00:13:45.770
could I actually don't
think you would want to.

00:13:45.770 --> 00:13:48.240
I think the reality is you
want to use that as your

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:52.290
jujitsu flip to get
over to the positive way

00:13:52.290 --> 00:13:54.700
of thinking, to get into
that positive habit loop.

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:56.088
To remind yourself that even if you're not

00:13:56.088 --> 00:13:58.440
good at it yet, you can get good at it.

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:01.130
That you're going to learn
by whatever you're doing.

00:14:01.130 --> 00:14:02.540
- And Rule Number 10, the last one

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:04.600
before a very special bonus clip

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:06.850
is Build the Life You Want.

00:14:06.850 --> 00:14:08.716
- I don't think people really realize

00:14:08.716 --> 00:14:10.602
we construct our lives.

00:14:10.602 --> 00:14:12.550
We build them from nothing.

00:14:12.550 --> 00:14:14.040
We decide what our goals are.

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:15.780
We decide what way to move.

00:14:15.780 --> 00:14:17.489
We decide who we're

00:14:17.489 --> 00:14:20.450
going to become and
what we're going to get.

00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:22.310
But it's a decision, it's a process.

00:14:22.310 --> 00:14:24.236
It isn't something that
somebody hands to you.

00:14:24.236 --> 00:14:27.240
And so, if you find that
your life is a misery

00:14:27.240 --> 00:14:29.940
understand that your life
is an exact reflection

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:30.864
of your choices.

00:14:30.864 --> 00:14:32.770
And if you want a different life

00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:35.430
you need only make a different choice.

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:37.007
But I know right now
many of you are thinking

00:14:37.007 --> 00:14:38.622
"But I don't know what way to go.

00:14:38.622 --> 00:14:40.359
I don't know what choice to make.

00:14:40.359 --> 00:14:41.390
I don't know what it is

00:14:41.390 --> 00:14:42.890
that I want to do.

00:14:42.890 --> 00:14:45.993
As as Roy Maurice Keane said,

00:14:45.993 --> 00:14:48.777
"I don't believe skill
was or ever will be the

00:14:48.777 --> 00:14:50.237
"result of coaches.

00:14:50.237 --> 00:14:52.107
"It is a result of a love affair

00:14:52.107 --> 00:14:54.672
"between the child and the ball."

00:14:54.672 --> 00:14:55.997
So ask yourself:

00:14:55.997 --> 00:14:58.730
what's that thing that you love?

00:14:58.730 --> 00:15:00.600
And don't judge yourself
if it was something you

00:15:00.600 --> 00:15:02.220
loved as a child that
people are telling you

00:15:02.220 --> 00:15:04.530
you couldn't make money
at, and it's that part

00:15:04.530 --> 00:15:06.280
of the equation that I
want to break for people.

00:15:06.280 --> 00:15:09.030
I want you to understand,
stop asking yourself

00:15:09.030 --> 00:15:11.130
what you can make a lot
of money at and start

00:15:11.130 --> 00:15:13.140
asking yourself, what would you enjoy?

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:15.960
What is that life that you
don't need to escape from?

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:18.840
What is the life that is your love?

00:15:18.840 --> 00:15:20.900
What is the thing that
as a kid you did whether

00:15:20.900 --> 00:15:22.000
people wanted you to or not?

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:22.833
What is the thing you

00:15:22.833 --> 00:15:25.100
would sneak out at night
to do because you weren't

00:15:25.100 --> 00:15:26.160
going to be stopped from doing it?

00:15:26.160 --> 00:15:28.780
Everybody has something
like that in their life.

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:31.060
Some spark of interest,
maybe long dormant.

00:15:31.060 --> 00:15:33.720
Maybe they've pushed
aside because they think

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:34.720
it's stupid.

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:37.460
Or maybe they failed once.

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:39.660
And they think they're bad at it.

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:43.610
Even though they love it,
that sting of the failure

00:15:43.610 --> 00:15:45.260
has convinced them to stop pursuing it.

00:15:45.260 --> 00:15:47.730
But at the end of the day, the only thing

00:15:47.730 --> 00:15:50.196
that matters is what
gives you that energy.

00:15:50.196 --> 00:15:52.280
At the end of the day,
the thing that matters is

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:53.480
what fills you with joy.

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:54.620
At the end of the day,

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:57.740
the only thing that matters is not success

00:15:57.740 --> 00:16:00.157
and sure as hell isn't money.

00:16:00.157 --> 00:16:02.970
It's how you feel

00:16:02.970 --> 00:16:05.336
about yourself when you're by yourself.

00:16:05.336 --> 00:16:06.610
It's the things that give you energy.

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:07.750
It's what you think about yourself.

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:09.130
It's how you react to the hard things.

00:16:09.130 --> 00:16:11.800
It's whether or not you push through.

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:14.540
And when you push through,
when you persevere,

00:16:14.540 --> 00:16:16.930
when you go down the
process of taking the time

00:16:16.930 --> 00:16:19.901
to structure your life,
to build it into something

00:16:19.901 --> 00:16:22.181
you want it to be, to
build it into something

00:16:22.181 --> 00:16:24.350
you're proud of, to
become the person that's

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:26.240
capable of the things you want to do,

00:16:26.240 --> 00:16:28.330
that can first fall in love
with something and do it for

00:16:28.330 --> 00:16:30.712
the love of it, not worry
about what other people think.

00:16:30.712 --> 00:16:32.970
If you hate your life I guarantee

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:35.610
the thing is you are trapped
by what other people think.

00:16:35.610 --> 00:16:37.002
You don't want to give it
up because somebody will

00:16:37.002 --> 00:16:38.910
think you're a failure,
you don't want to give

00:16:38.910 --> 00:16:40.550
it up because it's a paycheck.

00:16:40.550 --> 00:16:43.100
You don't want to give it
up because you're scared.

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:46.673
You're scared you don't
know what you'll do next.

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:49.400
But imagine a world where
for a second all you

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:51.270
thought about was what do you love?

00:16:51.270 --> 00:16:52.790
What do you enjoy in that moment?

00:16:52.790 --> 00:16:54.263
It doesn't matter if it
changes from day to day.

00:16:54.263 --> 00:16:55.423
What do you love?

00:16:55.423 --> 00:16:57.130
What fills you with joy?

00:16:57.130 --> 00:16:58.310
What gives you that energy?

00:16:58.310 --> 00:16:59.143
At the end of the day

00:16:59.143 --> 00:17:01.330
the only thing that we
all have is right now

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:04.737
this moment, it's what
you're experiencing.

00:17:04.737 --> 00:17:09.737
Loving what you do, how
you spend your time.

00:17:10.020 --> 00:17:12.040
That's the point of all of it.

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:13.797
The point of life is that.

00:17:13.797 --> 00:17:15.660
In each transient moment

00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:17.410
that passes by doing something

00:17:17.410 --> 00:17:18.613
that fills you with joy.

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:21.350
Nobody can give you that.

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:24.150
You've got to build that life.

00:17:24.150 --> 00:17:25.950
So go out.

00:17:25.950 --> 00:17:28.614
Figure out what it is that you want to do

00:17:28.614 --> 00:17:33.240
and brick by brick, have the courage to

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:34.890
build that life.

00:17:34.890 --> 00:17:36.360
- Now I've got a really special bonus clip

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:40.010
from Tom on how to start
asking how your wrong,

00:17:40.010 --> 00:17:41.530
that I think you're going to really enjoy.

00:17:41.530 --> 00:17:43.225
But before that, it's
time for the three point

00:17:43.225 --> 00:17:44.706
landing question, it's
time to move from just

00:17:44.706 --> 00:17:47.289
watching another video
to actually taking action

00:17:47.289 --> 00:17:49.220
in your life or in your business.

00:17:49.220 --> 00:17:50.200
And if you're bold,

00:17:50.200 --> 00:17:52.290
leave your replies in the comments below.

00:17:52.290 --> 00:17:54.040
Here we go.

00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:55.210
Question number one:

00:17:55.210 --> 00:17:58.080
What is the first step that
you need to take today?

00:17:58.080 --> 00:17:59.090
Number two:

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:00.442
What obstacle will you not

00:18:00.442 --> 00:18:01.480
let break you?

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:02.741
And number three:

00:18:02.741 --> 00:18:05.823
What are you going to
get better at this week?

00:18:09.320 --> 00:18:10.860
- People get stuck.

00:18:10.860 --> 00:18:12.710
They become so dogmatic.

00:18:12.710 --> 00:18:16.290
They become so convinced
that they're right.

00:18:16.290 --> 00:18:19.470
And that feeling of
being right gives them a

00:18:19.470 --> 00:18:20.866
sense of self-worth.

00:18:20.866 --> 00:18:22.680
And I'm telling you right

00:18:22.680 --> 00:18:26.263
now, with compassion because
I want to see you win.

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:30.860
Valuing yourself for
being right is a trap.

00:18:30.860 --> 00:18:34.050
Thinking of yourself as smart is a trap.

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:36.380
And I get it man, I know how good it feels

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:37.260
when you're right.

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:38.420
You had the right idea,

00:18:38.420 --> 00:18:41.760
it goes out and it wins,
that feels so good.

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:46.040
But if you can recognize
that over time it can

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:49.220
only paint you into a
corner, because the world

00:18:49.220 --> 00:18:51.050
changes, the world is adapting.

00:18:51.050 --> 00:18:52.967
The very thing that
makes humans the ultimate

00:18:52.967 --> 00:18:56.540
apex predator is that we adapt.

00:18:56.540 --> 00:18:57.373
Charles Darwin said,

00:18:57.373 --> 00:18:59.517
"It's not the strongest

00:18:59.517 --> 00:19:01.957
"of the species that survive,
nor the most intelligent

00:19:01.957 --> 00:19:05.280
"but rather the most adaptive to change."

00:19:05.280 --> 00:19:07.110
You've got to be willing
to change, you've always

00:19:07.110 --> 00:19:11.630
got to be willing to seek
out this confirming evidence.

00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:13.100
You've got to hunger for it, you've got

00:19:13.100 --> 00:19:14.920
to want to be proven wrong.

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:16.380
You've got to literally

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:18.270
invite people into your
world that are going

00:19:18.270 --> 00:19:20.400
to point out flaws in
your thinking because

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:23.343
your thinking has already taken
you as far as it's going to.

00:19:23.343 --> 00:19:24.990
So if you want to get farther,

00:19:24.990 --> 00:19:26.580
if you want to get to that next level,

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:28.930
you've got to stop valuing yourself

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:31.160
for who you are, what you
think, how smart you are,

00:19:31.160 --> 00:19:32.730
when you're right, when you're wrong,

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:34.090
all of that is irrelevant.

00:19:34.090 --> 00:19:35.500
You've got to value

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:39.800
yourself entirely on your willingness

00:19:39.800 --> 00:19:42.272
to admit that you're wrong.

00:19:42.272 --> 00:19:43.907
You've got to value

00:19:43.907 --> 00:19:47.200
yourself on your willingness to learn.

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:49.130
You've got to value
yourself on your willingness

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:52.713
to sit humbly at somebody's
feet and seek their wisdom.

00:19:52.713 --> 00:19:55.730
To not try to be the hero.

00:19:55.730 --> 00:19:56.863
But instead to try and be the one

00:19:56.863 --> 00:19:58.586
that collects the knowledge.

00:19:58.586 --> 00:20:01.220
When you can flip over into that

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:03.210
when you can value
yourself for a willingness

00:20:03.210 --> 00:20:07.070
to stare nakedly at your own inadequacies,

00:20:07.070 --> 00:20:09.640
you'll start to make progress in life.

00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:10.473
But no matter how far you've got,

00:20:10.473 --> 00:20:11.760
no matter how much you want,

00:20:11.760 --> 00:20:12.810
no matter how certain you are,

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:15.190
no matter how much the things you've done

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:18.280
in your life have proven to be correct,

00:20:18.280 --> 00:20:19.677
as Charlie Munger says,

00:20:19.677 --> 00:20:23.117
"You must force yourself
to consider arguments

00:20:23.117 --> 00:20:24.287
"on the other side."

00:20:25.210 --> 00:20:26.700
You can always reject them,

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:28.820
you can always look at
it, really think about it

00:20:28.820 --> 00:20:31.300
and say, "At the end of the
day, it's just not correct".

00:20:31.300 --> 00:20:33.030
But when you are trying to hold

00:20:33.030 --> 00:20:37.532
onto your ideas simply
because they're your ideas

00:20:37.532 --> 00:20:39.650
or simply because they worked in the past

00:20:39.650 --> 00:20:42.439
or simply because you like them,

00:20:42.439 --> 00:20:45.330
you will fall into a
trap of dogma and you'll

00:20:45.330 --> 00:20:47.285
no longer be able to
see fresh ideas and move

00:20:47.285 --> 00:20:48.570
in new directions.

00:20:48.570 --> 00:20:50.720
But if you're willing to acknowledge

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:52.560
that this world is constantly moving,

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:53.430
it's ever-changing.

00:20:53.430 --> 00:20:55.270
The only thing true about the future,

00:20:55.270 --> 00:20:57.940
always and forever, is that things change

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:00.210
and if you're thinking doesn't change,

00:21:00.210 --> 00:21:01.290
you'll never be able to keep up.

00:21:01.290 --> 00:21:03.570
So if you want to do
something extraordinary

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:06.773
with your life step number one,

00:21:07.670 --> 00:21:10.520
always seek out that
disconfirming evidence

00:21:10.520 --> 00:21:12.690
always look at arguments
from the other side.

00:21:12.690 --> 00:21:16.470
If you are able to do
that, then you'll always

00:21:16.470 --> 00:21:17.610
be able to stay ahead of the curve

00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:20.439
and aging won't be a problem
because you'll stay fresh

00:21:20.439 --> 00:21:22.063
in your mind.

00:21:23.050 --> 00:21:24.190
You become invincible when you

00:21:24.190 --> 00:21:26.750
bend and not break and
that's what this kind

00:21:26.750 --> 00:21:28.142
of mindset will allow you to have.

00:21:28.142 --> 00:21:31.207
So if you want to win,
stop thinking about how

00:21:31.207 --> 00:21:35.538
you're right and start
asking how you're wrong.

00:21:35.538 --> 00:21:38.090
- Raise your standards.

00:21:38.090 --> 00:21:42.457
- Apple, at the core,
it's core value, is that

00:21:42.457 --> 00:21:47.457
we believe that people
with passion can change

00:21:48.250 --> 00:21:49.083
the world for the better.

00:21:49.083 --> 00:21:51.165
- Not one drop of my self-worth depends

00:21:51.165 --> 00:21:53.483
on your acceptance of me.

00:21:59.020 --> 00:22:00.670
- If you liked this video
and want to learn more

00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:02.197
about the power of habit check out

00:22:02.197 --> 00:22:03.530
the video right next to me.

00:22:03.530 --> 00:22:05.010
I think you're going to enjoy it.

00:22:05.010 --> 00:22:07.470
Continue to believe
and I'll see you there.

00:22:07.470 --> 00:22:09.724
- We are what we repeatedly do.

00:22:09.724 --> 00:22:12.380
- Change doesn't just happen
at this level of behavior.

00:22:12.380 --> 00:22:14.250
But you have to change the environment.

00:22:14.250 --> 00:22:15.633
- Make a damn schedule!

